1
00:00:02,870 --> 00:00:04,380
Mitsuoka!

2
00:00:04,380 --> 00:00:05,630
Noren!

3
00:00:05,630 --> 00:00:07,380
Wait up!

4
00:00:07,710 --> 00:00:10,380
Tell us more
about what you said back there!

5
00:00:11,630 --> 00:00:13,340
Wait!

6
00:00:14,140 --> 00:00:15,720
Looks like we managed to lose them.

7
00:00:17,060 --> 00:00:19,140
Now then...

8
00:00:19,140 --> 00:00:20,140
What gives?!

9
00:00:20,520 --> 00:00:21,270
Sorry!

10
00:00:21,850 --> 00:00:25,110
The club activity I was really looking
forward to got totally wrecked.

11
00:00:25,480 --> 00:00:29,820
And before I knew it, all my
pent-up stress completely exploded.

12
00:00:29,820 --> 00:00:31,610
I know I messed up.

13
00:00:31,900 --> 00:00:33,360
Sorry.

14
00:00:34,110 --> 00:00:35,740
Hey, Juzo, doesn't this...

15
00:00:36,030 --> 00:00:37,620
technically mean mission accomplished?

16
00:00:37,620 --> 00:00:38,910
The hell it does!

17
00:00:38,910 --> 00:00:41,580
Marrying a kid
the same age as my daughter?

18
00:00:41,580 --> 00:00:43,000
I'd rather die!

19
00:00:43,500 --> 00:00:46,580
But, please! I know it's selfish,

20
00:00:46,580 --> 00:00:50,000
but could you pretend
to be my boyfriend for a while?

21
00:00:50,630 --> 00:00:51,550
Huh?

22
00:00:51,550 --> 00:00:54,050
Look, if people think
I already have a boyfriend,

23
00:00:54,050 --> 00:00:57,010
it should help prevent stuff
 like that from happening.

24
00:00:57,300 --> 00:00:58,560
Please!

25
00:01:01,270 --> 00:01:02,600
Fine.

26
00:01:03,270 --> 00:01:04,560
But this is...

27
00:01:04,560 --> 00:01:05,980
strictly pretend, got it?

28
00:02:36,030 --> 00:02:40,030
THE PACIFIER DUEL
SATURDAY, MAY 2nd

29
00:02:40,910 --> 00:02:41,530
Hey!

30
00:02:41,950 --> 00:02:43,330
Go buy us some bread!

31
00:02:43,700 --> 00:02:45,870
Oh, so this is how it goes.

32
00:02:45,870 --> 00:02:47,750
Are you listening to me?

33
00:02:48,580 --> 00:02:50,710
From now on, you'll run errands
for us every day,

34
00:02:50,710 --> 00:02:53,000
or you'll back off from Noren Mitsuoka.

35
00:02:53,000 --> 00:02:54,420
Pick one.

36
00:02:54,420 --> 00:02:55,710
What kind of choice is that?

37
00:03:00,340 --> 00:03:01,590
Don't let him get away!

38
00:03:01,590 --> 00:03:03,600
Beating them down would be easy...

39
00:03:03,850 --> 00:03:08,850
but I'm not about to get
 suspended over something so trivial.

40
00:03:12,150 --> 00:03:13,480
- Hey!
- We're on the third floor!

41
00:03:14,360 --> 00:03:15,820
What the...

42
00:03:21,490 --> 00:03:22,740
My apologies.

43
00:03:32,130 --> 00:03:33,420
Did you hear?

44
00:03:33,420 --> 00:03:35,800
Those two are apparently going out!

45
00:03:35,800 --> 00:03:39,130
Yeah, and because of that,
a bunch of guys have it out for him.

46
00:03:39,340 --> 00:03:40,510
Yikes!

47
00:03:40,510 --> 00:03:41,510
Poor guy.

48
00:03:42,550 --> 00:03:45,680
I said I'd do it
as long as it was just pretend,

49
00:03:45,680 --> 00:03:48,270
but is it gonna be like
 this the whole time?

50
00:03:48,270 --> 00:03:50,020
What a pain!

51
00:03:50,020 --> 00:03:51,520
- Rough day, Oga.
- Huh?

52
00:03:51,810 --> 00:03:54,310
Is it true that you're dating Noren?

53
00:03:54,310 --> 00:03:55,980
Takada and Baba...

54
00:03:55,980 --> 00:03:59,400
Seriously, though, nice job
getting away from those guys!

55
00:03:59,400 --> 00:04:00,400
You were watching?

56
00:04:00,400 --> 00:04:02,530
And all you did was watch?

57
00:04:02,530 --> 00:04:04,950
I mean, what were we supposed to do?

58
00:04:04,950 --> 00:04:06,780
Go get a teacher or something!

59
00:04:06,780 --> 00:04:10,250
We felt like you would handle it somehow.

60
00:04:10,250 --> 00:04:13,040
And you did, so what's the problem?

61
00:04:13,040 --> 00:04:13,670
Hey!

62
00:04:13,670 --> 00:04:14,790
Though...

63
00:04:15,250 --> 00:04:17,920
Honestly, things could 
still get way worse.

64
00:04:18,420 --> 00:04:19,670
Huh?

65
00:04:20,170 --> 00:04:24,340
Our school's a pretty famous
mega-school, y'know.

66
00:04:24,340 --> 00:04:28,060
There are high-spec guys
all over the place.

67
00:04:28,060 --> 00:04:29,890
And not just that.

68
00:04:30,180 --> 00:04:32,440
Among the upper crust, there's...

69
00:04:32,440 --> 00:04:35,230
an especially scary group 
called the Unicorns.

70
00:04:35,230 --> 00:04:38,820
They've got looks and personality, 
the whole package.

71
00:04:38,820 --> 00:04:41,690
And on top of that, every single one
of them has top-tier talent...

72
00:04:41,690 --> 00:04:43,860
and crazy charisma
in some field or another.

73
00:04:44,200 --> 00:04:48,330
Rumor has it all of them
are after Noren, too.

74
00:04:48,330 --> 00:04:51,040
Chances are they'll come
 after you sooner or later!

75
00:04:51,040 --> 00:04:52,460
And when that happens...

76
00:04:52,460 --> 00:04:53,790
well, good luck!

77
00:04:53,790 --> 00:04:54,580
Hey!

78
00:04:56,630 --> 00:04:58,800
It might be a good idea...

79
00:04:59,090 --> 00:05:00,630
to drop this "fake boyfriend" thing.

80
00:05:00,630 --> 00:05:01,460
Huh?

81
00:05:01,460 --> 00:05:02,170
Boss...

82
00:05:02,550 --> 00:05:05,090
You have no intention
of marrying Noren, right?

83
00:05:05,390 --> 00:05:06,760
Obviously not!

84
00:05:07,100 --> 00:05:09,810
Then there's no reason to keep this up.

85
00:05:09,810 --> 00:05:12,270
I do feel bad for her, but...

86
00:05:13,390 --> 00:05:16,400
And I've got one more
annoying update for you.

87
00:05:16,400 --> 00:05:17,020
What?

88
00:05:17,520 --> 00:05:21,820
It's about Mitsuoka Pharmaceuticals' 
wasp research and their de-aging drug.

89
00:05:21,820 --> 00:05:24,740
Apparently, the underworld
is after that secret, too.

90
00:05:25,110 --> 00:05:28,950
But they can't just take it
with threats or brute force.

91
00:05:28,950 --> 00:05:30,990
So, there's talk...

92
00:05:30,990 --> 00:05:34,460
that other organizations might send in
elite middle schooler operatives...

93
00:05:34,460 --> 00:05:36,420
to go undercover.

94
00:05:36,420 --> 00:05:40,090
All with the aim of becoming
Noren Mitsuoka's future husband.

95
00:05:40,500 --> 00:05:43,090
Meaning, she's gonna be targetted...

96
00:05:43,090 --> 00:05:45,760
by top-tier guys
from both sides of society.

97
00:05:45,760 --> 00:05:49,800
Unicorns, assassin agents, the whole deal.

98
00:05:49,800 --> 00:05:52,100
So, Boss, are throwing
 your hat in that ring, too?

99
00:05:56,770 --> 00:05:57,400
Huh?

100
00:05:58,230 --> 00:06:02,070
Yeah, you don't have to pretend
to be my boyfriend anymore.

101
00:06:02,070 --> 00:06:05,240
It seems to be causing you
a ton of trouble. Sorry.

102
00:06:05,240 --> 00:06:07,030
Yeah, but then...

103
00:06:07,030 --> 00:06:10,370
I mean, it's really something
I should deal with myself.

104
00:06:10,370 --> 00:06:13,410
I'll stop showing up at the home ec club.

105
00:06:13,830 --> 00:06:16,620
But hey, you should
still come by for ramen.

106
00:06:16,960 --> 00:06:19,540
I might vent to you
once in a while, though.

107
00:06:21,920 --> 00:06:22,920
Oh!

108
00:06:22,920 --> 00:06:24,880
On a date? Perfect timing!

109
00:06:25,510 --> 00:06:29,010
Quit running away already, Ogami.

110
00:06:29,010 --> 00:06:31,930
Nobody's okay with this, y'know.

111
00:06:31,930 --> 00:06:34,430
A gloomy loser like you
being her boyfriend?

112
00:06:34,770 --> 00:06:38,190
He's not my boyfriend anymore!
Can you quit this stupid crap already?

113
00:06:38,600 --> 00:06:40,150
Huh? Really?

114
00:06:40,150 --> 00:06:41,980
Then go out with me!

115
00:06:41,980 --> 00:06:43,480
What? No, thanks!

116
00:06:43,940 --> 00:06:46,030
Nobody asked you
to barge in here, so go to hell!

117
00:06:46,030 --> 00:06:47,990
Oh! Look, I'm not messing around!

118
00:06:47,990 --> 00:06:50,740
I'm strong, okay? I can protect you!

119
00:06:51,620 --> 00:06:53,910
I didn't ask! So, back off already!

120
00:06:53,910 --> 00:06:55,200
Aw, don't be so cold!

121
00:06:55,910 --> 00:06:58,210
No. We're still together.

122
00:06:58,210 --> 00:07:00,170
Keep your hands off my girl.

123
00:07:00,830 --> 00:07:01,750
Now get lost.

124
00:07:01,750 --> 00:07:02,880
- Huh?
- The hell?

125
00:07:03,170 --> 00:07:05,000
Wait, what? You're marrying her?

126
00:07:05,000 --> 00:07:07,800
Like hell I am!
We're just keeping the act going!

127
00:07:08,130 --> 00:07:10,010
Still, why, though?

128
00:07:10,010 --> 00:07:12,390
No reason.

129
00:07:12,390 --> 00:07:13,470
What?

130
00:07:13,470 --> 00:07:16,680
If I had to say, it's because
every damn kid keeps going,

131
00:07:16,680 --> 00:07:18,520
"No, don't," "It's fine" all the time!

132
00:07:19,390 --> 00:07:21,900
And we old guys are stubborn.
 That's why.

133
00:07:21,900 --> 00:07:23,820
If doing nothing makes kids worry about me,

134
00:07:23,820 --> 00:07:25,570
then I'll be a meddling 
pain in the ass.

135
00:07:25,570 --> 00:07:26,650
I don't care who shows up.

136
00:07:26,650 --> 00:07:29,450
If they're bad news, I'll swat
every last one of 'em away!

137
00:07:29,780 --> 00:07:31,780
What're you muttering about?

138
00:07:31,780 --> 00:07:34,200
I spar with grown men at the gym.

139
00:07:34,200 --> 00:07:36,830
You oughta think about
 who you're mouthing off to...

140
00:07:36,830 --> 00:07:37,750
before you try acting cool!

141
00:07:41,790 --> 00:07:48,210
I'm not saying I reject with the whole 
"men should protect women" thing,

142
00:07:48,210 --> 00:07:49,010
but for now...

143
00:07:49,800 --> 00:07:52,180
maybe you should spend
a little more time training.

144
00:07:54,140 --> 00:07:55,850
Ogami?

145
00:07:59,810 --> 00:08:01,980
Ogami, um...

146
00:08:02,440 --> 00:08:05,150
All right. I'll keep playing boyfriend
a little longer.

147
00:08:05,150 --> 00:08:07,900
I don't wanna eat good ramen and then
have to listen to you complain afterward.

148
00:08:09,400 --> 00:08:10,610
Thanks.

149
00:08:11,200 --> 00:08:12,150
But, um...

150
00:08:12,150 --> 00:08:14,280
that "keep your hands off my girl" line...

151
00:08:14,280 --> 00:08:16,370
Sorry, but wow, that was a huge turnoff.

152
00:08:16,740 --> 00:08:19,370
No middle schooler talks like that.

153
00:08:21,160 --> 00:08:21,960
So...

154
00:08:22,870 --> 00:08:25,840
that's Noren Mitsuoka and her boyfriend.

155
00:08:27,210 --> 00:08:31,340
With those moves, he seems like 
he might be in the same line of work as me.

156
00:08:34,430 --> 00:08:37,100
He may be tougher than expected...

157
00:08:37,600 --> 00:08:41,020
as a romantic rival on this job.

158
00:09:04,920 --> 00:09:06,250
Impressive.

159
00:09:07,000 --> 00:09:09,500
Your skills are sharp despite your age.

160
00:09:09,920 --> 00:09:12,670
You're a once-in-a-generation talent
for our organization.

161
00:09:13,010 --> 00:09:14,130
Thank you.

162
00:09:15,550 --> 00:09:17,220
Now for your next assignment.

163
00:09:18,260 --> 00:09:23,520
Infiltrate Noren Mitsuoka's middle school
and become her fiancé.

164
00:09:23,980 --> 00:09:25,350
I'm counting on you...

165
00:09:25,350 --> 00:09:27,230
Baby-Face Baby.

166
00:09:30,190 --> 00:09:32,110
Hey, Ogami...

167
00:09:32,940 --> 00:09:35,070
Aren't you, like, secretly super strong?

168
00:09:35,070 --> 00:09:35,700
Huh?

169
00:09:36,280 --> 00:09:37,370
No way.

170
00:09:37,370 --> 00:09:41,040
I've never been in a fight in my life.

171
00:09:41,410 --> 00:09:43,500
Really?

172
00:09:43,500 --> 00:09:47,380
Because the guy you scared off
the other day looked pretty tough to me.

173
00:09:47,750 --> 00:09:51,000
That was just a fluke, or,
I dunno, for all he looked the part...

174
00:09:51,500 --> 00:09:53,170
he was basically normal.

175
00:09:53,170 --> 00:09:54,670
"Normal"?

176
00:09:54,670 --> 00:09:58,470
So, does that mean you know
what "not normal" is like?

177
00:09:58,470 --> 00:10:00,680
No, I mean, I don't know.

178
00:10:00,930 --> 00:10:03,140
The boss is getting grilled
by a middle schooler!

179
00:10:03,850 --> 00:10:05,520
Well, whatever.

180
00:10:05,520 --> 00:10:07,520
This is just pretend dating anyway,

181
00:10:07,520 --> 00:10:09,980
so I'm not gonna say
you can't keep secrets or anything.

182
00:10:09,980 --> 00:10:12,780
But speaking of this
"fake boyfriend" thing...

183
00:10:13,190 --> 00:10:16,530
My dad randomly sent me
something yesterday.

184
00:10:18,950 --> 00:10:20,450
A fountain pen?

185
00:10:21,530 --> 00:10:23,410
What makes zero sense is...

186
00:10:23,410 --> 00:10:26,540
he told me to give this to Ogami,
the guy I'm dating right now.

187
00:10:27,250 --> 00:10:28,370
Why?

188
00:10:28,370 --> 00:10:29,670
No clue.

189
00:10:33,920 --> 00:10:35,510
Isn't he kinda hot?

190
00:10:35,510 --> 00:10:37,050
He's so tall!

191
00:10:37,470 --> 00:10:39,300
Look at how long his legs are!

192
00:10:39,300 --> 00:10:41,010
Check out his physique!

193
00:10:41,800 --> 00:10:44,770
Okay, class, I'd like to introduce
our new transfer student.

194
00:10:46,810 --> 00:10:48,190
Boss!

195
00:10:48,640 --> 00:10:49,520
Yeah.

196
00:10:49,850 --> 00:10:52,110
A transfer student at a time like this...

197
00:10:52,110 --> 00:10:53,570
And that presence...

198
00:10:53,900 --> 00:10:56,070
Looks like one really did show up.

199
00:10:56,740 --> 00:11:00,070
They sent in another pro...

200
00:11:00,490 --> 00:11:02,070
to become Noren's fiancé.

201
00:11:02,070 --> 00:11:04,290
This is Shin Kohazame.

202
00:11:05,660 --> 00:11:07,660
- Hell yes! A hottie!
- Everyone, be nice to him.

203
00:11:07,660 --> 00:11:10,620
Man, what a difference from Oga!
No, seriously, it's not even a contest!

204
00:11:11,170 --> 00:11:13,750
Now then, why don't you
give us a quick introduction?

205
00:11:18,300 --> 00:11:19,470
Afu?

206
00:11:22,930 --> 00:11:24,810
Duck?

207
00:11:35,570 --> 00:11:39,360
Wow, he's so nervous,
he completely choked.

208
00:11:39,700 --> 00:11:44,870
Um, okay. For now, why don't
 you sit next to Mitsuoka?

209
00:11:48,000 --> 00:11:50,460
Uh, nice to meet you.

210
00:11:56,840 --> 00:11:57,710
She's...

211
00:11:58,050 --> 00:11:59,720
She's so cute!

212
00:11:59,720 --> 00:12:02,760
Her picture did not do her justice!

213
00:12:02,760 --> 00:12:03,840
This is bad!

214
00:12:03,840 --> 00:12:06,470
I'm so nervous, I can barely even talk!

215
00:12:06,760 --> 00:12:09,770
There's no way
I can flirt with a girl this cute!

216
00:12:10,100 --> 00:12:12,190
But it's a job, so I have to!

217
00:12:12,190 --> 00:12:13,940
If I'm gonna talk without freaking out,

218
00:12:13,940 --> 00:12:16,610
I've got no choice
but to put that in my mouth!

219
00:12:18,110 --> 00:12:19,490
Huh?

220
00:12:19,820 --> 00:12:20,610
A letter?

221
00:12:20,610 --> 00:12:21,360
I LIKE YOU. I WANT TO TELL YOU THAT
IN PERSON,

222
00:12:21,360 --> 00:12:22,200
AND I'LL BE WAITING FOR YOU
IN THE COURTYARD AFTER SCHOOL.

223
00:12:22,200 --> 00:12:23,280
What?

224
00:12:23,280 --> 00:12:26,240
Did I really just get the sloppiest
love-letter approach ever?

225
00:12:30,250 --> 00:12:34,290
Jeez, when you're hot, people really
let you get away with anything, huh?

226
00:12:36,670 --> 00:12:39,210
A letter and then
an instant meet-up request.

227
00:12:39,210 --> 00:12:41,340
You want me there with you?

228
00:12:41,340 --> 00:12:42,720
Honestly, that'd help.

229
00:12:42,720 --> 00:12:45,050
That's basically the whole point
of the "fake boyfriend" thing.

230
00:12:45,050 --> 00:12:47,100
I knew you had a boyfriend.

231
00:12:47,100 --> 00:12:50,980
But if you bring him with you,
that does make this way harder. Jeez.

232
00:12:50,980 --> 00:12:51,600
Huh?

233
00:12:52,310 --> 00:12:56,860
Wait, that's Kohazame's voice,
but the vibe is completely different.

234
00:12:57,730 --> 00:12:59,980
No, hang on, what the heck is that?

235
00:13:00,400 --> 00:13:01,610
It's a pacifier.

236
00:13:01,610 --> 00:13:03,780
You make it sound like
 it's as normal as a mask!

237
00:13:04,070 --> 00:13:05,780
Sorry for freaking you out.

238
00:13:05,780 --> 00:13:10,450
I actually have extreme stage fright, 
but I calm down when I act like a baby.

239
00:13:10,450 --> 00:13:12,450
He's calmly saying the craziest nonsense!

240
00:13:13,040 --> 00:13:17,170
The underworld's full of weirdos,
but this guy's really something else.

241
00:13:17,170 --> 00:13:18,380
Yeah, he's out there.

242
00:13:18,710 --> 00:13:22,920
Anyway, can we talk
about what I wrote in the letter?

243
00:13:22,920 --> 00:13:25,890
Um, well, I'm already dating Ogami.

244
00:13:25,890 --> 00:13:27,220
I know.

245
00:13:27,220 --> 00:13:29,140
But I still have to say it.

246
00:13:30,140 --> 00:13:31,270
It was love at first sight.

247
00:13:32,600 --> 00:13:34,190
I really like you!

248
00:13:34,190 --> 00:13:35,600
Wow, pushy much?

249
00:13:35,980 --> 00:13:37,900
I know you already have a boyfriend.

250
00:13:37,900 --> 00:13:40,230
Even so, will you give me a chance?

251
00:13:41,730 --> 00:13:44,860
Looking at him again,
his eyes really are beautiful.

252
00:13:44,860 --> 00:13:48,240
When he looks at you like that,
your heart skips a beat.

253
00:13:48,620 --> 00:13:52,330
It's not just that his features
are handsome.

254
00:13:52,330 --> 00:13:56,000
There's this almost hypnotic kind
of sex appeal to him.

255
00:13:56,420 --> 00:13:57,330
Except...

256
00:13:57,790 --> 00:13:59,250
he's got a pacifier in his mouth!

257
00:13:59,880 --> 00:14:03,210
Well, okay, there are like ten different
things I could say here, but...

258
00:14:03,210 --> 00:14:04,130
Hey!

259
00:14:04,880 --> 00:14:07,640
Quit talking out of your ass, moron!

260
00:14:08,890 --> 00:14:12,100
For starters, you don't even like me
that much, do you?

261
00:14:12,850 --> 00:14:15,140
I'm not saying
love at first sight never happens,

262
00:14:15,140 --> 00:14:17,600
and sure, sometimes things move fast
out of nowhere.

263
00:14:17,600 --> 00:14:19,060
But this isn't that.

264
00:14:19,060 --> 00:14:22,400
What ticks me off is that it feels
like you're being made to do this!

265
00:14:22,980 --> 00:14:24,900
Yeah, it's rough
dealing with confessions...

266
00:14:24,900 --> 00:14:26,900
but if someone tells me
how they really feel...

267
00:14:26,900 --> 00:14:29,280
I make a point
of giving them a real answer.

268
00:14:29,280 --> 00:14:31,740
But if somebody comes at me
with some joke of a confession,

269
00:14:31,740 --> 00:14:33,830
like they're making fun
of other people's feelings,

270
00:14:33,830 --> 00:14:35,330
I make a point of decking them!

271
00:14:36,660 --> 00:14:37,790
What a...

272
00:14:40,130 --> 00:14:42,670
What a direct, strong person!

273
00:14:43,210 --> 00:14:44,880
I'm really in love!

274
00:14:47,420 --> 00:14:48,800
Good boy, good boy.

275
00:14:48,800 --> 00:14:53,010
If a girl like this did that for me,
I could die happy!

276
00:14:54,890 --> 00:14:56,310
No, sorry!

277
00:14:56,310 --> 00:14:57,640
I'm really sorry!

278
00:14:58,100 --> 00:14:59,810
You were totally right about all of it.

279
00:15:00,480 --> 00:15:02,860
And I like you. For real this time.

280
00:15:02,860 --> 00:15:05,280
If you can tell when someone's lying,
you can also tell when they mean it.

281
00:15:07,280 --> 00:15:09,070
So, anyway, your boyfriend...

282
00:15:09,070 --> 00:15:10,280
Ogami.

283
00:15:10,280 --> 00:15:11,870
"Ogami," right.

284
00:15:14,120 --> 00:15:14,870
Just like that?

285
00:15:16,700 --> 00:15:17,750
He got behind me?

286
00:15:18,120 --> 00:15:20,290
You're in the business, too, aren't you?

287
00:15:20,290 --> 00:15:24,590
I never thought a sudden confession
like that would actually work.

288
00:15:24,920 --> 00:15:28,880
My plan was to make an impression first,
then ease into it little by little.

289
00:15:28,880 --> 00:15:29,550
But...

290
00:15:29,930 --> 00:15:31,050
I've changed my mind.

291
00:15:33,140 --> 00:15:35,140
Putting Noren's position as fiancée
on the line...

292
00:15:35,810 --> 00:15:37,270
I challenge you to a duel.

293
00:15:37,270 --> 00:15:39,020
Huh? A duel?

294
00:15:39,020 --> 00:15:40,060
That.

295
00:15:40,690 --> 00:15:45,070
That fountain pen is proof
of who is the official fiancé.

296
00:15:45,770 --> 00:15:50,030
Once a duel is issued,
it has to be accepted.

297
00:15:50,450 --> 00:15:53,070
The guidelines
have already been announced.

298
00:15:53,070 --> 00:15:54,280
Wait, what is that supposed to mean?

299
00:15:54,830 --> 00:15:56,290
Since when?

300
00:15:56,700 --> 00:16:00,000
So if you lose, does the boyfriend role 
automatically changes hands?

301
00:16:00,000 --> 00:16:03,500
Jeez! This just keeps getting
more and more annoying!

302
00:16:04,170 --> 00:16:07,590
Basically, you decided you wanted
to steal her quick and easy, huh?

303
00:16:07,590 --> 00:16:08,670
Exactly.

304
00:16:08,670 --> 00:16:10,420
Sigh...

305
00:16:10,880 --> 00:16:12,630
Please give Noren to me.

306
00:16:13,050 --> 00:16:15,680
I don't give a damn about duels
or whatever else.

307
00:16:15,680 --> 00:16:17,770
But I'm not handing Noren over!

308
00:16:17,770 --> 00:16:19,680
You're way too freaky for your own good.

309
00:16:19,680 --> 00:16:20,350
MITSUOKA PHARMACEUTICALS

310
00:16:20,350 --> 00:16:24,690
So, whoever's holding the fountain pen
at the end is the fiancé...

311
00:16:24,980 --> 00:16:26,190
is that it?

312
00:16:26,190 --> 00:16:27,780
That is brutal!

313
00:16:27,780 --> 00:16:29,320
Hang in there, Oga!

314
00:16:29,320 --> 00:16:30,650
This is no laughing matter!

315
00:16:30,990 --> 00:16:33,110
Noren, are you okay?

316
00:16:33,110 --> 00:16:35,530
No, I am not okay!

317
00:16:35,530 --> 00:16:38,740
I hate the idea of people making this
huge spectacle out of fighting over me!

318
00:16:38,740 --> 00:16:39,910
I feel like I'm gonna puke!

319
00:16:40,830 --> 00:16:44,290
And Ogami's only doing this
because I asked him to fake it.

320
00:16:44,290 --> 00:16:47,630
It's not like I was planning
to date anyone in the first place!

321
00:16:47,630 --> 00:16:48,840
Ogami...

322
00:16:49,210 --> 00:16:50,710
It's okay, Master.

323
00:16:51,380 --> 00:16:53,220
I'm in this now.

324
00:16:53,220 --> 00:16:55,970
I'm not gonna lose
no matter what kind of match this is.

325
00:16:58,390 --> 00:17:00,770
They're saying it's a duel
over Noren Mitsuoka!

326
00:17:01,100 --> 00:17:02,850
The one that was posted online?

327
00:17:02,850 --> 00:17:04,980
No way! They're really doing it?

328
00:17:05,310 --> 00:17:07,060
The match lasts one hour.

329
00:17:07,060 --> 00:17:09,820
My objective is to make you
put this pacifier in your mouth.

330
00:17:10,150 --> 00:17:13,320
If you can escape without having it
crammed in, then you win.

331
00:17:14,320 --> 00:17:15,610
Pacifier!

332
00:17:16,030 --> 00:17:17,530
What kind of stupid contest is this?

333
00:17:17,830 --> 00:17:19,870
A pacifier? What?

334
00:17:19,870 --> 00:17:21,160
I don't get it!

335
00:17:21,160 --> 00:17:23,660
Why is he sucking on one
in the first place?

336
00:17:24,080 --> 00:17:26,210
I love you, Noren.

337
00:17:26,210 --> 00:17:27,460
I really mean it.

338
00:17:27,840 --> 00:17:30,170
So, if I win this duel...

339
00:17:30,800 --> 00:17:32,260
I want to use your lap...

340
00:17:32,260 --> 00:17:33,260
Good boy, good boy.

341
00:17:33,260 --> 00:17:34,340
...as a pillow.

342
00:17:34,340 --> 00:17:35,880
Sorry. Not happening.

343
00:17:38,800 --> 00:17:40,220
Let's get started.

344
00:17:40,640 --> 00:17:43,600
When the last grain falls,
exactly one hour will have passed.

345
00:17:43,600 --> 00:17:45,600
Yeah, yeah, let's do this already.

346
00:17:45,600 --> 00:17:46,650
Begin!

347
00:17:50,610 --> 00:17:51,530
Boss!

348
00:17:51,530 --> 00:17:52,990
Even bracing myself, that was close.

349
00:17:53,530 --> 00:17:56,110
Weirdo factor aside,
his skills are the real deal.

350
00:17:56,780 --> 00:17:57,610
It started!

351
00:17:57,610 --> 00:17:58,950
Oh, man!

352
00:18:01,580 --> 00:18:03,410
Uh, isn't this plain bad?

353
00:18:03,830 --> 00:18:06,170
Trying to run away
without blowing your cover and all!

354
00:18:06,580 --> 00:18:07,670
In other words, for one hour...

355
00:18:08,130 --> 00:18:10,380
I've gotta dodge his attacks
in the most pathetic way possible!

356
00:18:10,380 --> 00:18:11,750
In a weird way, that's kind of pro!

357
00:18:15,340 --> 00:18:16,220
Is this luck?

358
00:18:16,680 --> 00:18:18,180
He's actually dodging his strikes!

359
00:18:19,010 --> 00:18:20,800
Even before I had this younger body,

360
00:18:20,800 --> 00:18:23,100
it'd been a long time
since I'd faced anyone this good.

361
00:18:23,100 --> 00:18:24,640
He's really strong.

362
00:18:24,930 --> 00:18:26,140
Which is exactly why...

363
00:18:26,560 --> 00:18:28,850
a match where I lose
if he gets a pacifier in my mouth...

364
00:18:29,150 --> 00:18:30,060
What the hell?

365
00:18:34,860 --> 00:18:37,070
Shh!

366
00:18:42,580 --> 00:18:45,290
After Noren turned me down,
I thought about it.

367
00:18:45,290 --> 00:18:48,000
What exactly is the difference between us?

368
00:18:48,330 --> 00:18:50,000
And then it hit me.

369
00:18:50,290 --> 00:18:51,540
One of us is a baby...

370
00:18:51,540 --> 00:18:52,750
and one of us...

371
00:18:53,050 --> 00:18:53,750
isn't!

372
00:18:54,050 --> 00:18:55,460
What the hell are you talking about?

373
00:19:06,680 --> 00:19:08,480
Just try putting it in your mouth,

374
00:19:08,480 --> 00:19:10,020
and you'll get why it's so great!

375
00:19:10,020 --> 00:19:12,440
And once we're both babies...

376
00:19:12,730 --> 00:19:13,980
I'll be superior!

377
00:19:14,320 --> 00:19:16,440
No good! I still have no idea
what you're on about!

378
00:19:18,280 --> 00:19:19,490
More than anything...

379
00:19:19,490 --> 00:19:21,490
I'm in love with Noren!

380
00:19:21,990 --> 00:19:23,950
Are your feelings for her
stronger than mine?

381
00:19:25,410 --> 00:19:27,290
My feelings for Noren...

382
00:19:27,290 --> 00:19:28,540
My...

383
00:19:29,160 --> 00:19:30,250
Nope.

384
00:19:30,250 --> 00:19:31,670
Not even one millimeter.

385
00:19:31,670 --> 00:19:32,960
I'm a grown man.

386
00:19:33,460 --> 00:19:36,460
I only took this on because 
I got stubbornand dug in my heels.

387
00:19:37,130 --> 00:19:38,130
Hah...

388
00:19:38,130 --> 00:19:40,800
So, if I lose, worst case,
it can't be helped.

389
00:19:40,800 --> 00:19:41,970
Is that all this is?

390
00:19:45,930 --> 00:19:48,560
TO PAPA

391
00:19:48,560 --> 00:19:49,230
Papa!

392
00:19:49,770 --> 00:19:51,480
No. Wrong.

393
00:19:52,480 --> 00:19:53,860
It's more than that.

394
00:19:55,570 --> 00:19:57,190
There's about one minute left.

395
00:19:59,700 --> 00:20:00,650
There they are!

396
00:20:00,650 --> 00:20:02,110
Over there!

397
00:20:05,370 --> 00:20:06,410
He threw it!

398
00:20:06,410 --> 00:20:07,580
Huh? Is it over?

399
00:20:08,040 --> 00:20:10,080
Yeah, this ends it.

400
00:20:10,540 --> 00:20:11,330
Except...

401
00:20:17,630 --> 00:20:20,010
I never said that was the only pacifier.

402
00:20:20,300 --> 00:20:21,260
A trap!

403
00:20:21,260 --> 00:20:23,840
A whole bunch of them are flying at him!

404
00:20:29,180 --> 00:20:31,980
He left me an escape route on purpose!

405
00:20:32,640 --> 00:20:34,690
He's gonna land on a rake!

406
00:20:34,690 --> 00:20:36,150
One of those things where,
if you step on it...

407
00:20:36,150 --> 00:20:38,400
...the handle whips up and 
smacks you right in the face!

408
00:20:38,980 --> 00:20:41,150
And there's a pacifier
attached to the end of it!

409
00:20:41,490 --> 00:20:45,410
- And he can't block it!
- It's going in his mouth for sure!

410
00:20:46,160 --> 00:20:47,160
Wha...

411
00:20:49,370 --> 00:20:50,700
It stopped!

412
00:20:50,700 --> 00:20:51,790
How?

413
00:20:57,670 --> 00:20:59,710
So, when he jumped back...

414
00:21:00,590 --> 00:21:02,170
he'd already...

415
00:21:02,630 --> 00:21:04,430
thrown the wood carving knives?

416
00:21:06,300 --> 00:21:08,310
He made it the whole hour!

417
00:21:08,310 --> 00:21:09,970
How'd he do that at the end?

418
00:21:09,970 --> 00:21:11,730
Ogami wins!

419
00:21:12,810 --> 00:21:14,350
Unbelievable!

420
00:21:14,350 --> 00:21:15,690
My love...

421
00:21:16,060 --> 00:21:17,730
actually lost!

422
00:21:18,360 --> 00:21:19,520
Sorry.

423
00:21:19,860 --> 00:21:22,440
I don't know if mine's stronger
than yours...

424
00:21:23,320 --> 00:21:26,370
but I've got feelings for Noren, too.

425
00:21:26,820 --> 00:21:28,700
They're just nothing like yours.

426
00:21:30,700 --> 00:21:31,950
I only just realized it.

427
00:21:32,910 --> 00:21:36,960
I'd been projecting Kozue onto Noren.

428
00:21:37,540 --> 00:21:39,920
There's so much I couldn't do for Kozue.

429
00:21:40,670 --> 00:21:42,460
Maybe it's just self-satisfaction.

430
00:21:42,920 --> 00:21:47,640
Even so, I don't want Noren
to end up unhappy.

431
00:23:21,150 --> 00:23:23,980
Yeah, he's definitely pretty down.

432
00:23:25,320 --> 00:23:27,940
But I don't know how to deal
with two boys dueling over me, either.

433
00:23:27,940 --> 00:23:28,900
HOME EC ROOM

434
00:23:28,900 --> 00:23:31,700
Um, our new club member is...

435
00:23:32,370 --> 00:23:34,200
Shin Kohazame.

436
00:23:34,910 --> 00:23:35,540
Hey!

437
00:23:35,790 --> 00:23:37,910
I'm not giving up, Noren!

438
00:23:37,910 --> 00:23:40,000
Uh, no, please do give up.

